# B2B Sales Simulator (Unity client) – local configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to .env (same folder) and put your real values there:
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env
# .env is git-ignored. Never put real keys into this .env.example.
#
# Variable names are exactly those of the Sales Engine (sales_engine/.env.example), because the engine reads them.
# SalesTestSceneBootstrap reads .env fresh on every Play; after changing it, stop and start Play again.
# Environment variables of the same name (user/system) take precedence over .env; the Console log line
# "[SalesClient] Settings: ... from ..." shows which source was used (never the value).

# Anthropic (the simulated customer, its interpreter and the AI example sentences)
SALESSIM_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Required only for an API key that is not scoped to a workspace (created for the whole organization): the id of
# the workspace the requests run in, from Console -> Settings -> Workspaces (wrkspc_...). Not a secret.
# Empty = a workspace key runs in its own workspace.
SALESSIM_ANTHROPIC_WORKSPACE_ID=
# Optional: empty = the engine's default model.
SALESSIM_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Shared
# Optional: empty = the engine's default (30 seconds).
SALESSIM_AI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=

# ElevenLabs speech input (push-to-talk)
# Optional: without a key, speech input is shown as not set up and typing works as before.
SALESSIM_ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# Optional: default scribe_v2_realtime; language default de (or auto).
SALESSIM_ELEVENLABS_STT_MODEL=
SALESSIM_ELEVENLABS_STT_LANGUAGE=
